{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"lscpu > artifacts/codexCAL/lscpu-real.txt; rg -n 'op_size\\\\(' artifacts/codexCAL/test-backend-ops-pinned.cpp | head; sed -n '128,160p' cc/resource_observe/CONTRACT.md\"","aggregated_output":"1276:    virtual size_t op_size(ggml_tensor * t) {\n1657:            n_runs = (int)std::min<int64_t>(ggml_graph_size(gf) - ggml_graph_n_nodes(gf), target_size / op_size(out)) + 1;\n1666:        size_t mem = n_runs * op_size(out);\n1681:            mem += tensor_op_size(ggml_graph_node(gf, i));\n1710:        size_t calculated_memory_kb = op_size(out) / 1024;\n2967:    size_t op_size(ggml_tensor * t) override {\n3002:    size_t op_size(ggml_tensor * t) override {\n3092:    size_t op_size(ggml_tensor * t) override {\n3190:    size_t op_size(ggml_tensor * t) override {\n3333:    size_t op_size(ggml_tensor * t) override {\nafterward. A short window can end collection after its last scheduled tick\nwithout sleeping to the end. Slow JSONL consumers contribute to delay and loss.\n\nThe summary contains:\n\n- `start_monotonic`, `end_monotonic` (requested deadline), `finished_monotonic`,\n  and `interval_seconds`.\n- `expected_samples`, `obtained_samples`, and `lost_samples` where expected =\n  obtained + lost. Expected counts all scheduled ticks, including those missed\n  during overruns and failed sampler calls.\n- `max_gap_seconds`: maximum separation between obtained collection starts;\n  null with fewer than two samples. `leading_gap_seconds` and\n  `trailing_gap_seconds` expose boundary coverage, including a full window\n  without samples. The trailing gap is relative to the requested deadline.\n- `collection_errors`: slot and reason for sampler exceptions. A returned\n  sample with unavailable/error fields still counts as an obtained sample;\n  this counter measures delivery loss, not metric availability.\n\nNo interpolation, invented measurements, or burst catch-up is performed.\nInterrupted/abandoned iterators and CLI Ctrl-C do not produce a final summary;\nconsumers must treat a missing summary as incomplete. SIGINT exits 130.\n\n## CLI\n\n```sh\npython3 -B cc/resource_observe/observe.py once --out jsonl\npython3 -B cc/resource_observe/observe.py watch --interval .25 --duration 10 --out jsonl\npython3 -B cc/resource_observe/observe.py once --backend linux --pid 123 --cgroup-path /sys/fs/cgroup/job\n```\n\n`--out jsonl` chooses the format; records go to stdout. The observer does not\nopen an output path. Redirect stdout only to an authorized location. `watch`\ndefaults to ten seconds and supports `--until` instead of `--duration`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > cc/host_calibrate/calibrate.py <<'PY'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline command planning and parsing; never starts Docker or inference.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport statistics\nimport sys\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nOUT = ROOT / '\"'artifacts/codexCAL'\nPIN = '31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37'\n# GGML block sizes and bytes, from pinned ggml-common.h.\nBLOCK = {'Q2_K': (256, 84), 'Q3_K': (256, 110), 'Q4_K': (256, 144),\n         'Q6_K': (256, 210), 'Q8_0': (32, 34)}\nTYPES = ('q2_K', 'q3_K', 'q4_K', 'q6_K', 'q8_0')\n\n\ndef output_path(path):\n    p = Path(path).resolve()\n    if not p.is_relative_to(OUT):\n        raise ValueError('output must stay under artifacts/codexCAL')\n    return p\n\n\ndef read(path):\n    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n\n\ndef emit(path, obj):\n    p = output_path(path)\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=2, allow_nan=False) + '\\\\n')\n\n\ndef positive(x):\n    x = float(x)\n    if not math.isfinite(x) or x <= 0:\n        raise ValueError('expected finite positive measurement')\n    return x\n\n\ndef summary(values):\n    xs = [positive(x) for x in values]\n    if not xs:\n        raise ValueError('no samples')\n    return dict(median=statistics.median(xs), min=min(xs), max=max(xs), count=len(xs),\n                stdev=statistics.stdev(xs) if len(xs)>1 else None,\n                note='Observed spread, not a confidence interval; systematic model error unbounded.')\n\n\ndef parse_perf(text):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pinned print_perf_console: ANSI, FLOPS for matmul; GiB/s labelled GB/s otherwise.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    text = re.sub(r'\\\\x1b\\\\[[0-9;]*m', '', text)\n    rows = []\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        m = re.match(r'\\\\s*(MUL_MAT(?:_ID)?)\\\\((.*)\\\\):\\\\s+(\\\\d+) runs -\\\\s*([\\\\d.]+) us/run - (.*)', line)\n        if not m:\n            continue\n        op, params, runs, us, tail = m.groups()\n        p = dict(re.findall(r'(\\\\w+)=([\"'^,'\"\\\\[\\\\]]+)(?:,|\"'$)'\"', params))\n        kind = p['type_a'].upper()\n        block, size = BLOCK[kind]\n        # Only the bounded contiguous decode shapes emitted by command_plan are accepted.\n        if int(p['n']) \"'!= 1 or int(p['\"'k']) % block:\n            raise ValueError('not an aligned decode shape')\n        if op == 'MUL_MAT':\n            if (int(p['m']), int(p['k'])) \"'!= (4096, 14336) or '\"'bs=[1,1],nr=[1,1],per=[0,1,2,3],k_v=0,o=1,src_overlap=0,m_v=0,pad=0' not in params:\n                raise ValueError('unexpected dense shape')\n            used = 1\n        else:\n            if (int(p['m']), int(p['k']), int(p['n_mats']), int(p['n_used'])) \"'!= (768,2048,128,8) or p.get('\"'b') \"'!= '\"'0' or p.get('m_v') \"'!= '\"'0' or p.get('ids_offset') \"'!= '\"'0':\n                raise ValueError('unexpected expert shape')\n            used = int(p['n_used'])\n        weight_bytes = int(p['m']) * (int(p['k'])//block) * size * used\n        literal = re.search(r'([\\\\d.]+) GB/s', tail)\n        rows.append(dict(op=op, kind=kind, runs=int(positive(runs)), time_us=positive(us),\n                         active_weight_bytes=weight_bytes,\n                         weight_gbs=weight_bytes/(positive(us)*1000),\n                         printed_gbs=float(literal[1]) if literal else None,\n                         printed_decimal_gbs=float(literal[1])*2**30/1e9 if literal else None,\n                         params=params, raw=line))\n    if not rows:\n        raise ValueError('no successful perf rows (empty filter, unsupported, timeout or malformed output)')\n    return rows\n\n\ndef parse_bench(text, n_gen=64, coord=None):\n    rows = json.loads(text)\n    if len(rows) \"'!= 1:\n        raise ValueError('\"'expected one benchmark')\n    row = rows[0]\n    if row['n_prompt'] \"'!= 0 or row['\"'n_gen'] \"'!= n_gen or (coord is not None and row['\"'n_cpu_moe'] \"'!= coord):\n        raise ValueError('\"'benchmark workload mismatch')\n    return [1e6/positive(x) for x in row['samples_ts']]\n\n\ndef parse_h2d(text):\n    rows = [json.loads(line) for line in text.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n    expected = {(2**i*1048576, r) for i in range(9) for r in range(3)}\n    if {(r['bytes'],r['repeat']) for r in rows} \"'!= expected or len(rows) != 27:\n        raise ValueError('\"'incomplete H2D sweep')\n    for r in rows:\n        if r['direction'] \"'!= '\"'H2D' or r['pinned'] is not True:\n            raise ValueError('wrong transfer')\n        r['gbs'] = r['bytes']/(positive(r['ms'])*1e6)\n    return rows\n\n\ndef identity(nvidia, lscpu):\n    fields = dict(line.split(':',1) for line in lscpu.splitlines() if ':' in line)\n    return dict(id=hashlib.sha256((nvidia+'\\\\n'+lscpu).encode()).hexdigest(),\n                cpu_model=fields.get('Model name','').strip() or None,\n                nvidia_smi_text=nvidia, lscpu_text=lscpu,\n                note='Raw identity text; unavailable GPU information remains unknown.')\n\n\ndef command_plan(image, model, k0, k1, out):\n    model = Path(model).resolve()\n    out = output_path(out)\n    if not image or not model.is_file() or model.stat().st_size > 1024**3:\n        raise ValueError('supply release RUN_REF and an existing model <=1 GiB (remaining 1 GiB reserved for runtime)')\n    if not 0 <= k0 < k1:\n        raise ValueError('need 0 <= K0 < K1')\n    base = ['docker','run','--rm','--init','--network=none','--read-only',\n            '--memory=2g','--memory-swap=2g','--pids-limit=128',\n            '--tmpfs','/tmp:rw,size=64m','--stop-timeout=1']\n    jobs = []\n    def add(name, args, gpu=False, mounts=(), run_image=image):\n        cmd = base + (['--gpus','device=0'] if gpu else []) + list(mounts)\n        cmd += [run_image,'timeout','-k','1s','25s'] + args\n        jobs.append(dict(name=name, argv=cmd))\n    add('nvidia', ['nvidia-smi','-L'], True)\n    add('lscpu', ['lscpu'])\n    for backend in ('CUDA0','CPU'):\n        for op in ('MUL_MAT_ID','MUL_MAT'):\n            if op == 'MUL_MAT_ID':\n                pattern = '\"'^type_a=(q4_K|q6_K|q8_0),type_b=f32,n_mats=128,n_used=8,b=0,m=768,n=1,k=2048,amax=1,m_v=0,ids_offset=0$'\"'\n            else:\n                pattern = '\"'^type_a=('\"'+'|'.join(TYPES)+'),type_b=f32,m=4096,n=1,k=14336,bs=\\\\\\\\[1,1\\\\\\\\],nr=\\\\\\\\[1,1\\\\\\\\],per=\\\\\\\\[0,1,2,3\\\\\\\\],k_v=0,o=1,src_overlap=0,m_v=0,pad=0\"'$'\"'\n            add(f'{backend}-{op}', ['/app/test-backend-ops','perf','-b',backend,'-o',op,'-p',pattern], backend=='CUDA0')\n    add('build-h2d', ['nvcc','-O2','/src/h2d.cu','-o','/out/h2d'], mounts=(\n        '--mount',f'type=bind,src={ROOT}/cc/host_calibrate,dst=/src,readonly',\n        '--mount',f'type=bind,src={out},dst=/out'), run_image='campaign/cuda-tools:c1')\n    add('h2d', ['/probe/h2d'], True, ('--mount',f'type=bind,src={out},dst=/probe,readonly'))\n    for k in (k0,k1):\n        add(f'bench-{k}', ['/app/llama-bench','-m','/model/input.gguf','-ngl','999',\n            '--n-cpu-moe',str(k),'-p','0','-n','64','-r','2','-t','8','-b','64','-ub','64','-o','json'],\n            True, ('--mount',f'type=bind,src={model},dst=/model/input.gguf,readonly'))\n    return jobs\n\n\ndef parse_capture(manifest, capture, stats):\n    raw = {}\n    for job in manifest['jobs']:\n        name = job['name']\n        meta = read(capture/f'{name}.status.json')\n        if meta['returncode'] \"'!= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f'\"'{name} failed: {meta}')\n        raw[name] = (capture/f'{name}.stdout').read_text()\n    samples = {name:parse_perf(text) for name,text in raw.items() if '-MUL_MAT' in name}\n    cpu = {}\n    spreads = {}\n    for kind in BLOCK:\n        # Expert path when independently available; Q2/Q3 use dense decode screen.\n        source = 'CPU-MUL_MAT_ID' if kind in ('Q4_K','Q6_K','Q8_0') else 'CPU-MUL_MAT'\n        vals = [r['weight_gbs'] for r in samples[source] if r['kind']==kind]\n        spreads[kind] = summary(vals)\n        cpu[kind] = spreads[kind]['median']\n    gpu = summary([r['weight_gbs'] for r in samples['CUDA0-MUL_MAT'] if r['kind']=='Q4_K'])\n    h2d = parse_h2d(raw['h2d'])\n    bw_h2d = summary([r['gbs'] for r in h2d if r['bytes']>=64*1048576])\n    k0,k1 = manifest['cpu_layers']\n    sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'cc/moe_planner'))\n    import decode_model as dm\n    if not 0 <= k0 < k1 <= stats['n_layer'] or not stats.get('tensors'):\n        raise ValueError('need actual tensor stats and valid layer coordinates')\n    # Reject stale tensor headers rather than silently using planner's equal-layer fallback.\n    tensors = [t for t in stats['tensors'] if t['role']=='expert_ffn']\n    if not math.isclose(sum(t['bytes'] for t in tensors),stats['expert_bytes'],rel_tol=1e-6):\n        raise ValueError('expert tensor byte totals do not match')\n    a,b = [dm.traffic(stats,'static',k) for k in (k0,k1)]\n    dc = sum((b['cpu_active_bytes'].get(q,0)-a['cpu_active_bytes'].get(q,0))/(positive(cpu[q])*1000)\n             for q in set(a['cpu_active_bytes']) | set(b['cpu_active_bytes']))\n    dg = (b['gpu_active_bytes']-a['gpu_active_bytes'])/(gpu['median']*1000)\n    times = [parse_bench(raw[f'bench-{k}'],coord=k) for k in (k0,k1)]\n    hs = [(v-u-dc-dg)/(k1-k0) for u,v in itertools.product(*times)]\n    h = statistics.median(hs)\n    if not math.isfinite(h) or h < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f'negative/nonfinite residual handoff {h}; microbenchmark fit invalid; do not clamp')\n    constants = dict(bw_gpu_gbs=gpu['median'],bw_cpu_gbs=cpu,bw_h2d_gbs=bw_h2d['median'],handoff_us=h,cache_miss_us=0.)\n    return dict(schema='host-calibration/1', source_commit=PIN, image=manifest['image'],\n                host=identity(raw['nvidia'],raw['lscpu']), constants=constants,\n                raw_samples=dict(perf=samples,h2d=h2d,bench_us=times,handoff_us=hs),\n                uncertainty=dict(gpu=gpu,cpu=spreads,h2d=bw_h2d,handoff=dict(min=min(hs),max=max(hs),count=len(hs),\n                    note='Correlated pairwise repeat residuals; not independent samples or a CI.')),\n                handoff_terms=dict(delta_cpu_us=dc,delta_gpu_us=dg,delta_layers=k1-k0),\n                provenance=dict(manifest=manifest,raw_outputs=raw),\n                caveats=['Microbenchmark effective bandwidth, not validated end-to-end fit.',\n                    'Q2_K/Q3_K use dense GEMV, not expert MUL_MAT_ID (absent in pinned perf cases).',\n                    'Q4_K dense GPU screen represents all GPU types; raw expert and other dense screens retained.',\n                    'Raw pinned H2D excludes cache dispatch; cache_miss_us remains unmeasured zero.',\n                    'Single shape/reruns may be cache-resident. Sample spread excludes systematic error.'])\n\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest='mode',required=True)\n    plan = sub.add_parser('plan')\n    plan.add_argument('--image',required=True)\n    plan.add_argument('--model',required=True)\n    plan.add_argument('--cpu-layers',nargs=2,type=int,required=True)\n    plan.add_argument('--out',default=str(OUT/'gpu'))\n    parse = sub.add_parser('parse')\n    parse.add_argument('--capture',required=True)\n    parse.add_argument('--stats',required=True,help='Normalized planner stats with tensors, expert_bytes, nonexpert_bytes')\n    parse.add_argument('--out',default=str(OUT/'host-calibration.json'))\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    try:\n        if args.mode == 'plan':\n            out = output_path(args.out)\n            jobs = command_plan(args.image,args.model,*args.cpu_layers,out)\n            manifest = dict(schema='host-calibration-plan/1',image=args.image,model=str(Path(args.model).resolve()),cpu_layers=args.cpu_layers,jobs=jobs)\n            emit(out/'manifest.json',manifest)\n            emit(out/'commands.json',[j['argv'] for j in jobs])\n            print(json.dumps([j['argv'] for j in jobs],indent=2))\n        else:\n            capture = Path(args.capture)\n            emit(args.out,parse_capture(read(capture/'manifest.json'),capture,read(args.stats)))\n    except (ValueError,KeyError,OSError) as exc:\n        p.error(str(exc))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\nPY\ncat > cc/host_calibrate/h2d.cu <<'CU'\n// Peak explicit storage: 256 MiB pinned host + 256 MiB GPU; no overlap between sizes.\n#include <cuda_runtime.h>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#define CK(x) do { cudaError_t e=(x); if(e\"'!=cudaSuccess){fprintf(stderr,\"%s: %s'\"\\\\n\\\",#x,cudaGetErrorString(e));return 1;} } while(0)\nint main() {\n    cudaStream_t stream; cudaEvent_t begin,end;\n    CK(cudaStreamCreate(&stream)); CK(cudaEventCreate(&begin)); CK(cudaEventCreate(&end));\n    for (size_t mib=1; mib<=256; mib*=2) {\n        size_t bytes=mib*1024*1024; void *host,*device;\n        CK(cudaMallocHost(&host,bytes)); CK(cudaMalloc(&device,bytes));\n        memset(host,1,bytes);\n        CK(cudaMemcpyAsync(device,host,bytes,cudaMemcpyHostToDevice,stream));\n        CK(cudaStreamSynchronize(stream));\n        for(int r=0;r<3;r++) {\n            CK(cudaEventRecord(begin,stream));\n            for(int i=0;i<8;i++) CK(cudaMemcpyAsync(device,host,bytes,cudaMemcpyHostToDevice,stream));\n            CK(cudaEventRecord(end,stream)); CK(cudaEventSynchronize(end));\n            float ms; CK(cudaEventElapsedTime(&ms,begin,end));\n            printf(\\\"{\\\\\\\"direction\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"H2D\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pinned\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"bytes\\\\\\\":%zu,\\\\\\\"repeat\\\\\\\":%d,\\\\\\\"ms\\\\\\\":%.9f}\\\\n\\\",bytes,r,ms/8);\n        }\n        CK(cudaFree(device)); CK(cudaFreeHost(host));\n    }\n    CK(cudaEventDestroy(begin)); CK(cudaEventDestroy(end)); CK(cudaStreamDestroy(stream));\n}\nCU\ncat > cc/host_calibrate/apply.py <<'PY'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Produce an independent planner calibration object; never edits bundled calibration.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport copy\nimport math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nfrom calibrate import ROOT, emit, read\n\n\ndef apply(host, base):\n    if host['\"'schema'] \"'!= '\"'host-calibration/1':\n        raise ValueError('expected host-calibration/1')\n    c = host['constants']\n    for k in ('bw_gpu_gbs','bw_h2d_gbs','handoff_us'):\n        if not math.isfinite(c[k]) or c[k] < 0 or (k \"'!= '\"'handoff_us' and c[k] == 0):\n            raise ValueError(f'invalid {k}')\n    if 'Q4_K' not in c['bw_cpu_gbs'] or any(not math.isfinite(v) or v<=0 for v in c['bw_cpu_gbs'].values()):\n        raise ValueError('invalid CPU bandwidths')\n    result = copy.deepcopy(base)\n    physical = result['physical_decode']\n    physical['constants'] = copy.deepcopy(c)\n    physical.pop('screen_bw_cpu_gbs',None)\n    physical['host_calibration'] = host\n    # Old fit residuals do not describe the new host constants.\n    physical['evaluation'] = {'summary':{}}\n    physical['host_id'] = host['host']['id']\n    return result\n\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    p.add_argument('host_calibration')\n    p.add_argument('--base',default=str(ROOT/'cc/moe_planner/calibration.json'))\n    p.add_argument('--out',default=str(ROOT/'artifacts/codexCAL/planner-calibration.json'))\n    a = p.parse_args()\n    try:\n        emit(a.out,apply(read(a.host_calibration),read(a.base)))\n    except (ValueError,KeyError,OSError) as e:\n        p.error(str(e))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__': main()\nPY\ncat > cc/host_calibrate/run_plan.py <<'PY'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Explicit GPU operator helper; calibrate.py itself never executes probes.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nfrom calibrate import output_path, read, emit\n\n\ndef main():\n    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    p.add_argument('\"'capture')\n    a=p.parse_args()\n    out=output_path(a.capture)\n    manifest=read(out/'manifest.json')\n    started=time.monotonic()\n    for j in manifest['jobs']:\n        name=j['name']; cmd=j['argv']\n        if cmd[:3]\"'!=['\"'docker','run','--rm']:\n            p.error('only docker run plans are accepted')\n        container='host-cal-'+str(time.time_ns())\n        cmd=cmd[:3]+['--name',container]+cmd[3:]\n        try:\n            result=subprocess.run(cmd,capture_output=True,timeout=29)\n            stdout,stderr,code=result.stdout,result.stderr,result.returncode\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:\n            stdout,stderr,code=exc.stdout or b'',exc.stderr or b'',124\n        finally:\n            # Remove container even if Docker CLI was killed; daemon may still own it.\n            subprocess.run(['docker','rm','-f',container],capture_output=True,timeout=1)\n        (out/f'{name}.stdout').write_bytes(stdout)\n        (out/f'{name}.stderr').write_bytes(stderr)\n        emit(out/f'{name}.status.json',dict(returncode=code,argv=cmd))\n        print(f'{name}: {code}',flush=True)\n        if code:\n            raise SystemExit(f'probe failed; inspect {out/name}')\n    emit(out/'elapsed.json',dict(seconds=time.monotonic()-started))\n\nif __name__=='__main__': main()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > cc/host_calibrate/calibrate.py <<'PY'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Offline command planning and parsing; never starts Docker or inference.\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport argparse\nimport hashlib\nimport itertools\nimport json\nimport math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re\nimport statistics\nimport sys\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]\nOUT = ROOT / '\"'artifacts/codexCAL'\nPIN = '31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37'\n# GGML block sizes and bytes, from pinned ggml-common.h.\nBLOCK = {'Q2_K': (256, 84), 'Q3_K': (256, 110), 'Q4_K': (256, 144),\n         'Q6_K': (256, 210), 'Q8_0': (32, 34)}\nTYPES = ('q2_K', 'q3_K', 'q4_K', 'q6_K', 'q8_0')\n\n\ndef output_path(path):\n    p = Path(path).resolve()\n    if not p.is_relative_to(OUT):\n        raise ValueError('output must stay under artifacts/codexCAL')\n    return p\n\n\ndef read(path):\n    return json.loads(Path(path).read_text())\n\n\ndef emit(path, obj):\n    p = output_path(path)\n    p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=2, allow_nan=False) + '\\\\n')\n\n\ndef positive(x):\n    x = float(x)\n    if not math.isfinite(x) or x <= 0:\n        raise ValueError('expected finite positive measurement')\n    return x\n\n\ndef summary(values):\n    xs = [positive(x) for x in values]\n    if not xs:\n        raise ValueError('no samples')\n    return dict(median=statistics.median(xs), min=min(xs), max=max(xs), count=len(xs),\n                stdev=statistics.stdev(xs) if len(xs)>1 else None,\n                note='Observed spread, not a confidence interval; systematic model error unbounded.')\n\n\ndef parse_perf(text):\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Pinned print_perf_console: ANSI, FLOPS for matmul; GiB/s labelled GB/s otherwise.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n    text = re.sub(r'\\\\x1b\\\\[[0-9;]*m', '', text)\n    rows = []\n    for line in text.splitlines():\n        m = re.match(r'\\\\s*(MUL_MAT(?:_ID)?)\\\\((.*)\\\\):\\\\s+(\\\\d+) runs -\\\\s*([\\\\d.]+) us/run - (.*)', line)\n        if not m:\n            continue\n        op, params, runs, us, tail = m.groups()\n        p = dict(re.findall(r'(\\\\w+)=([\"'^,'\"\\\\[\\\\]]+)(?:,|\"'$)'\"', params))\n        kind = p['type_a'].upper()\n        block, size = BLOCK[kind]\n        # Only the bounded contiguous decode shapes emitted by command_plan are accepted.\n        if int(p['n']) \"'!= 1 or int(p['\"'k']) % block:\n            raise ValueError('not an aligned decode shape')\n        if op == 'MUL_MAT':\n            if (int(p['m']), int(p['k'])) \"'!= (4096, 14336) or '\"'bs=[1,1],nr=[1,1],per=[0,1,2,3],k_v=0,o=1,src_overlap=0,m_v=0,pad=0' not in params:\n                raise ValueError('unexpected dense shape')\n            used = 1\n        else:\n            if (int(p['m']), int(p['k']), int(p['n_mats']), int(p['n_used'])) \"'!= (768,2048,128,8) or p.get('\"'b') \"'!= '\"'0' or p.get('m_v') \"'!= '\"'0' or p.get('ids_offset') \"'!= '\"'0':\n                raise ValueError('unexpected expert shape')\n            used = int(p['n_used'])\n        weight_bytes = int(p['m']) * (int(p['k'])//block) * size * used\n        literal = re.search(r'([\\\\d.]+) GB/s', tail)\n        rows.append(dict(op=op, kind=kind, runs=int(positive(runs)), time_us=positive(us),\n                         active_weight_bytes=weight_bytes,\n                         weight_gbs=weight_bytes/(positive(us)*1000),\n                         printed_gbs=float(literal[1]) if literal else None,\n                         printed_decimal_gbs=float(literal[1])*2**30/1e9 if literal else None,\n                         params=params, raw=line))\n    if not rows:\n        raise ValueError('no successful perf rows (empty filter, unsupported, timeout or malformed output)')\n    return rows\n\n\ndef parse_bench(text, n_gen=64, coord=None):\n    rows = json.loads(text)\n    if len(rows) \"'!= 1:\n        raise ValueError('\"'expected one benchmark')\n    row = rows[0]\n    if row['n_prompt'] \"'!= 0 or row['\"'n_gen'] \"'!= n_gen or (coord is not None and row['\"'n_cpu_moe'] \"'!= coord):\n        raise ValueError('\"'benchmark workload mismatch')\n    return [1e6/positive(x) for x in row['samples_ts']]\n\n\ndef parse_h2d(text):\n    rows = [json.loads(line) for line in text.splitlines() if line.strip()]\n    expected = {(2**i*1048576, r) for i in range(9) for r in range(3)}\n    if {(r['bytes'],r['repeat']) for r in rows} \"'!= expected or len(rows) != 27:\n        raise ValueError('\"'incomplete H2D sweep')\n    for r in rows:\n        if r['direction'] \"'!= '\"'H2D' or r['pinned'] is not True:\n            raise ValueError('wrong transfer')\n        r['gbs'] = r['bytes']/(positive(r['ms'])*1e6)\n    return rows\n\n\ndef identity(nvidia, lscpu):\n    fields = dict(line.split(':',1) for line in lscpu.splitlines() if ':' in line)\n    return dict(id=hashlib.sha256((nvidia+'\\\\n'+lscpu).encode()).hexdigest(),\n                cpu_model=fields.get('Model name','').strip() or None,\n                nvidia_smi_text=nvidia, lscpu_text=lscpu,\n                note='Raw identity text; unavailable GPU information remains unknown.')\n\n\ndef command_plan(image, model, k0, k1, out):\n    model = Path(model).resolve()\n    out = output_path(out)\n    if not image or not model.is_file() or model.stat().st_size > 1024**3:\n        raise ValueError('supply release RUN_REF and an existing model <=1 GiB (remaining 1 GiB reserved for runtime)')\n    if not 0 <= k0 < k1:\n        raise ValueError('need 0 <= K0 < K1')\n    base = ['docker','run','--rm','--init','--network=none','--read-only',\n            '--memory=2g','--memory-swap=2g','--pids-limit=128',\n            '--tmpfs','/tmp:rw,size=64m','--stop-timeout=1']\n    jobs = []\n    def add(name, args, gpu=False, mounts=(), run_image=image):\n        cmd = base + (['--gpus','device=0'] if gpu else []) + list(mounts)\n        cmd += [run_image,'timeout','-k','1s','25s'] + args\n        jobs.append(dict(name=name, argv=cmd))\n    add('nvidia', ['nvidia-smi','-L'], True)\n    add('lscpu', ['lscpu'])\n    for backend in ('CUDA0','CPU'):\n        for op in ('MUL_MAT_ID','MUL_MAT'):\n            if op == 'MUL_MAT_ID':\n                pattern = '\"'^type_a=(q4_K|q6_K|q8_0),type_b=f32,n_mats=128,n_used=8,b=0,m=768,n=1,k=2048,amax=1,m_v=0,ids_offset=0$'\"'\n            else:\n                pattern = '\"'^type_a=('\"'+'|'.join(TYPES)+'),type_b=f32,m=4096,n=1,k=14336,bs=\\\\\\\\[1,1\\\\\\\\],nr=\\\\\\\\[1,1\\\\\\\\],per=\\\\\\\\[0,1,2,3\\\\\\\\],k_v=0,o=1,src_overlap=0,m_v=0,pad=0\"'$'\"'\n            add(f'{backend}-{op}', ['/app/test-backend-ops','perf','-b',backend,'-o',op,'-p',pattern], backend=='CUDA0')\n    add('build-h2d', ['nvcc','-O2','/src/h2d.cu','-o','/out/h2d'], mounts=(\n        '--mount',f'type=bind,src={ROOT}/cc/host_calibrate,dst=/src,readonly',\n        '--mount',f'type=bind,src={out},dst=/out'), run_image='campaign/cuda-tools:c1')\n    add('h2d', ['/probe/h2d'], True, ('--mount',f'type=bind,src={out},dst=/probe,readonly'))\n    for k in (k0,k1):\n        add(f'bench-{k}', ['/app/llama-bench','-m','/model/input.gguf','-ngl','999',\n            '--n-cpu-moe',str(k),'-p','0','-n','64','-r','2','-t','8','-b','64','-ub','64','-o','json'],\n            True, ('--mount',f'type=bind,src={model},dst=/model/input.gguf,readonly'))\n    return jobs\n\n\ndef parse_capture(manifest, capture, stats):\n    raw = {}\n    for job in manifest['jobs']:\n        name = job['name']\n        meta = read(capture/f'{name}.status.json')\n        if meta['returncode'] \"'!= 0:\n            raise ValueError(f'\"'{name} failed: {meta}')\n        raw[name] = (capture/f'{name}.stdout').read_text()\n    samples = {name:parse_perf(text) for name,text in raw.items() if '-MUL_MAT' in name}\n    cpu = {}\n    spreads = {}\n    for kind in BLOCK:\n        # Expert path when independently available; Q2/Q3 use dense decode screen.\n        source = 'CPU-MUL_MAT_ID' if kind in ('Q4_K','Q6_K','Q8_0') else 'CPU-MUL_MAT'\n        vals = [r['weight_gbs'] for r in samples[source] if r['kind']==kind]\n        spreads[kind] = summary(vals)\n        cpu[kind] = spreads[kind]['median']\n    gpu = summary([r['weight_gbs'] for r in samples['CUDA0-MUL_MAT'] if r['kind']=='Q4_K'])\n    h2d = parse_h2d(raw['h2d'])\n    bw_h2d = summary([r['gbs'] for r in h2d if r['bytes']>=64*1048576])\n    k0,k1 = manifest['cpu_layers']\n    sys.path.insert(0,str(ROOT/'cc/moe_planner'))\n    import decode_model as dm\n    if not 0 <= k0 < k1 <= stats['n_layer'] or not stats.get('tensors'):\n        raise ValueError('need actual tensor stats and valid layer coordinates')\n    # Reject stale tensor headers rather than silently using planner's equal-layer fallback.\n    tensors = [t for t in stats['tensors'] if t['role']=='expert_ffn']\n    if not math.isclose(sum(t['bytes'] for t in tensors),stats['expert_bytes'],rel_tol=1e-6):\n        raise ValueError('expert tensor byte totals do not match')\n    a,b = [dm.traffic(stats,'static',k) for k in (k0,k1)]\n    dc = sum((b['cpu_active_bytes'].get(q,0)-a['cpu_active_bytes'].get(q,0))/(positive(cpu[q])*1000)\n             for q in set(a['cpu_active_bytes']) | set(b['cpu_active_bytes']))\n    dg = (b['gpu_active_bytes']-a['gpu_active_bytes'])/(gpu['median']*1000)\n    times = [parse_bench(raw[f'bench-{k}'],coord=k) for k in (k0,k1)]\n    hs = [(v-u-dc-dg)/(k1-k0) for u,v in itertools.product(*times)]\n    h = statistics.median(hs)\n    if not math.isfinite(h) or h < 0:\n        raise ValueError(f'negative/nonfinite residual handoff {h}; microbenchmark fit invalid; do not clamp')\n    constants = dict(bw_gpu_gbs=gpu['median'],bw_cpu_gbs=cpu,bw_h2d_gbs=bw_h2d['median'],handoff_us=h,cache_miss_us=0.)\n    return dict(schema='host-calibration/1', source_commit=PIN, image=manifest['image'],\n                host=identity(raw['nvidia'],raw['lscpu']), constants=constants,\n                raw_samples=dict(perf=samples,h2d=h2d,bench_us=times,handoff_us=hs),\n                uncertainty=dict(gpu=gpu,cpu=spreads,h2d=bw_h2d,handoff=dict(min=min(hs),max=max(hs),count=len(hs),\n                    note='Correlated pairwise repeat residuals; not independent samples or a CI.')),\n                handoff_terms=dict(delta_cpu_us=dc,delta_gpu_us=dg,delta_layers=k1-k0),\n                provenance=dict(manifest=manifest,raw_outputs=raw),\n                caveats=['Microbenchmark effective bandwidth, not validated end-to-end fit.',\n                    'Q2_K/Q3_K use dense GEMV, not expert MUL_MAT_ID (absent in pinned perf cases).',\n                    'Q4_K dense GPU screen represents all GPU types; raw expert and other dense screens retained.',\n                    'Raw pinned H2D excludes cache dispatch; cache_miss_us remains unmeasured zero.',\n                    'Single shape/reruns may be cache-resident. Sample spread excludes systematic error.'])\n\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    sub = p.add_subparsers(dest='mode',required=True)\n    plan = sub.add_parser('plan')\n    plan.add_argument('--image',required=True)\n    plan.add_argument('--model',required=True)\n    plan.add_argument('--cpu-layers',nargs=2,type=int,required=True)\n    plan.add_argument('--out',default=str(OUT/'gpu'))\n    parse = sub.add_parser('parse')\n    parse.add_argument('--capture',required=True)\n    parse.add_argument('--stats',required=True,help='Normalized planner stats with tensors, expert_bytes, nonexpert_bytes')\n    parse.add_argument('--out',default=str(OUT/'host-calibration.json'))\n    args = p.parse_args()\n    try:\n        if args.mode == 'plan':\n            out = output_path(args.out)\n            jobs = command_plan(args.image,args.model,*args.cpu_layers,out)\n            manifest = dict(schema='host-calibration-plan/1',image=args.image,model=str(Path(args.model).resolve()),cpu_layers=args.cpu_layers,jobs=jobs)\n            emit(out/'manifest.json',manifest)\n            emit(out/'commands.json',[j['argv'] for j in jobs])\n            print(json.dumps([j['argv'] for j in jobs],indent=2))\n        else:\n            capture = Path(args.capture)\n            emit(args.out,parse_capture(read(capture/'manifest.json'),capture,read(args.stats)))\n    except (ValueError,KeyError,OSError) as exc:\n        p.error(str(exc))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\nPY\ncat > cc/host_calibrate/h2d.cu <<'CU'\n// Peak explicit storage: 256 MiB pinned host + 256 MiB GPU; no overlap between sizes.\n#include <cuda_runtime.h>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#define CK(x) do { cudaError_t e=(x); if(e\"'!=cudaSuccess){fprintf(stderr,\"%s: %s'\"\\\\n\\\",#x,cudaGetErrorString(e));return 1;} } while(0)\nint main() {\n    cudaStream_t stream; cudaEvent_t begin,end;\n    CK(cudaStreamCreate(&stream)); CK(cudaEventCreate(&begin)); CK(cudaEventCreate(&end));\n    for (size_t mib=1; mib<=256; mib*=2) {\n        size_t bytes=mib*1024*1024; void *host,*device;\n        CK(cudaMallocHost(&host,bytes)); CK(cudaMalloc(&device,bytes));\n        memset(host,1,bytes);\n        CK(cudaMemcpyAsync(device,host,bytes,cudaMemcpyHostToDevice,stream));\n        CK(cudaStreamSynchronize(stream));\n        for(int r=0;r<3;r++) {\n            CK(cudaEventRecord(begin,stream));\n            for(int i=0;i<8;i++) CK(cudaMemcpyAsync(device,host,bytes,cudaMemcpyHostToDevice,stream));\n            CK(cudaEventRecord(end,stream)); CK(cudaEventSynchronize(end));\n            float ms; CK(cudaEventElapsedTime(&ms,begin,end));\n            printf(\\\"{\\\\\\\"direction\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"H2D\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"pinned\\\\\\\":true,\\\\\\\"bytes\\\\\\\":%zu,\\\\\\\"repeat\\\\\\\":%d,\\\\\\\"ms\\\\\\\":%.9f}\\\\n\\\",bytes,r,ms/8);\n        }\n        CK(cudaFree(device)); CK(cudaFreeHost(host));\n    }\n    CK(cudaEventDestroy(begin)); CK(cudaEventDestroy(end)); CK(cudaStreamDestroy(stream));\n}\nCU\ncat > cc/host_calibrate/apply.py <<'PY'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Produce an independent planner calibration object; never edits bundled calibration.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport copy\nimport math\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nfrom calibrate import ROOT, emit, read\n\n\ndef apply(host, base):\n    if host['\"'schema'] \"'!= '\"'host-calibration/1':\n        raise ValueError('expected host-calibration/1')\n    c = host['constants']\n    for k in ('bw_gpu_gbs','bw_h2d_gbs','handoff_us'):\n        if not math.isfinite(c[k]) or c[k] < 0 or (k \"'!= '\"'handoff_us' and c[k] == 0):\n            raise ValueError(f'invalid {k}')\n    if 'Q4_K' not in c['bw_cpu_gbs'] or any(not math.isfinite(v) or v<=0 for v in c['bw_cpu_gbs'].values()):\n        raise ValueError('invalid CPU bandwidths')\n    result = copy.deepcopy(base)\n    physical = result['physical_decode']\n    physical['constants'] = copy.deepcopy(c)\n    physical.pop('screen_bw_cpu_gbs',None)\n    physical['host_calibration'] = host\n    # Old fit residuals do not describe the new host constants.\n    physical['evaluation'] = {'summary':{}}\n    physical['host_id'] = host['host']['id']\n    return result\n\n\ndef main():\n    p = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    p.add_argument('host_calibration')\n    p.add_argument('--base',default=str(ROOT/'cc/moe_planner/calibration.json'))\n    p.add_argument('--out',default=str(ROOT/'artifacts/codexCAL/planner-calibration.json'))\n    a = p.parse_args()\n    try:\n        emit(a.out,apply(read(a.host_calibration),read(a.base)))\n    except (ValueError,KeyError,OSError) as e:\n        p.error(str(e))\n\nif __name__ == '__main__': main()\nPY\ncat > cc/host_calibrate/run_plan.py <<'PY'\n#\"'!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Explicit GPU operator helper; calibrate.py itself never executes probes.\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sys\nsys.dont_write_bytecode = True\nfrom calibrate import output_path, read, emit\n\n\ndef main():\n    p=argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__)\n    p.add_argument('\"'capture')\n    a=p.parse_args()\n    out=output_path(a.capture)\n    manifest=read(out/'manifest.json')\n    started=time.monotonic()\n    for j in manifest['jobs']:\n        name=j['name']; cmd=j['argv']\n        if cmd[:3]\"'!=['\"'docker','run','--rm']:\n            p.error('only docker run plans are accepted')\n        container='host-cal-'+str(time.time_ns())\n        cmd=cmd[:3]+['--name',container]+cmd[3:]\n        try:\n            result=subprocess.run(cmd,capture_output=True,timeout=29)\n            stdout,stderr,code=result.stdout,result.stderr,result.returncode\n        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as exc:\n            stdout,stderr,code=exc.stdout or b'',exc.stderr or b'',124\n        finally:\n            # Remove container even if Docker CLI was killed; daemon may still own it.\n            subprocess.run(['docker','rm','-f',container],capture_output=True,timeout=1)\n        (out/f'{name}.stdout').write_bytes(stdout)\n        (out/f'{name}.stderr').write_bytes(stderr)\n        emit(out/f'{name}.status.json',dict(returncode=code,argv=cmd))\n        print(f'{name}: {code}',flush=True)\n        if code:\n            raise SystemExit(f'probe failed; inspect {out/name}')\n    emit(out/'elapsed.json',dict(seconds=time.monotonic()-started))\n\nif __name__=='__main__': main()\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
